WEBVTT

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.860
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:31.200
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:38.940
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:45.080
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.860
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:57.630
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.600
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:12.540
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:20.210
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.430
Why didn't you wake
me up sooner?!

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.970
I tried to.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.900
It's your fault you
didn't get up.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:40.840
Oh!

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.540
You're an ice-woman!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.940
I'm leaving.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.470
Wait! Wait for me!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.550
Oops.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:56.350
I'm off! Good
luck today!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.920
Wait for me,
Miyuki!

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:11.940
FILE. 49
INSPECTOR
KINOSHITA

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.080
Done!

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.480
Here's my report!

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.950
Thank you. If only you would always
write them up as quickly.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:35.220
What do you mean? You make it sound
like I'm a slacker or something.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.660
Aren't you?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.190
I pull through when
I have to!

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.170
Wow! Natsumi's actually
written up a report.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.470
Well, maybe it's
going to rain.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.670
And then it's dangerous,
with the tires slipping.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.740
Not you, too.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.150
I have to say, I feel
kind of lonely...

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.280
Aoi.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.980
Aoi.
...since Toukairin won't be around.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.990
He doesn't talk much, but you
definitely feel his presence.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.820
He's probably so caught up with climbing
mountains, that he's forgotten about us.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.260
Forget about people
who aren't here.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.630
Let's just do
our best.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.150
Inspector Kinoshita. I've
been waiting for you.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.660
Chief. I'd like to speak to everyone,
in the meeting room.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:52.600
I understand. You heard the Inspector.
To the main meeting room!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.600
I'm Kaoruko
Kinoshita...

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.910
...and starting today
I'll be...

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.950
...heading up a special investigation
team here at Bokuto.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:06.080
I'm sure you're
all aware of...

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:08.420
...a recent wave of
luxury car thefts.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.510
Lately some of these thefts have occurred
within Bokuto's jurisdiction.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:16.790
It's likely the same
perpetrator.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.400
Headquarters has decided
to create...

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.990
...a special investigation
unit based at Bokuto.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.930
I have a question.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.400
Yes?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.240
You say there'll be a new
investigation unit.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.640
Where are we going to find
the people to staff it?

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:36.440
She's right. We have our hands
full with our current workload.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.680
That's for sure.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.380
I've put in 10 hours of overtime this month.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.750
Me, too.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.180
Of course...

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.920
...this won't interfere in any way
with your daily responsibilities.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:54.090
On the other hand, you'll have to be
very thorough on your patrols.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:05:01.570
The bike patrol will meet at the station
at 7 p.m., and depart in pairs at 7;30.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.840
Regular street patrols
will begin at 8.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.110
My God, she's deciding
every move we make.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.840
No kidding. That's not something
that goes so smoothly.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.820
There's always things
that'll throw us off.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.180
These shifts will be in place
until further notice.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.930
In addition, some people will
be assigned special duties.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.300
Sergeant Kobayakawa.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.170
Sergeant Kobayakawa.
Uh... Yes?

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.800
You'll be in charge of getting
on the computer...

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:35.340
...and trying to come up with a simulation of
the thieves' movements and patterns.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.840
Who, me?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:41.070
You'll be provided with a
high-speed workstation.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:45.580
A special network's been set up so you
can access Headquarters' databases.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.050
Do you need anything else?

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.050
No.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.550
I object! Miyuki...

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.350
...I mean, Sergeant Kobayakawa
is my partner!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.420
I can't carry out my
duties without her.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.160
Sergeant Tsujimoto.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.160
There's no need
to worry.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:05.500
I'm going to fill in
as your partner.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.300
If it's all right
with you.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.680
Wow, what
a setup.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.950
Inspector Kinoshita's very
serious about this.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:25.990
She wants to catch
those criminals.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.560
Indeed. We have to
do our very best.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.190
She's gone to
all this effort.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:38.570
Still, I wonder if Natsumi will be all
right on duty with an Inspector.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.230
They don't seem to be
very compatible.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:45.570
Well, no matter what happens, I can't
see her fighting with an Inspector.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.700
At least, I don't
think.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.260
Do you dislike being on patrol
with me that much?

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.900
No, that's
not true.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.060
I've heard all about how
you and Kobayakawa...

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.460
...have solved a good number
of cases together.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.760
Well, it wasn't really
that many!

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.240
But I wonder if that justifies feeling
satisfied with yourself.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.350
No matter how good a team you two are,
you're not going to be together forever.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:23.750
One day, Kobayakawa will
have to go her way...

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:28.340
...and you'll have
to go yours.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.860
Natsumi!

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:34.120
Natsumi!
Natsumi's here!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.920
Hi, Natsumi!

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:40.220
Hi! That's a nice way
to greet someone!

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.590
We know the
rules!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.640
We're not little kids,
you know!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.170
Sorry! Sorry!

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.780
Sorry! Sorry!
Hey, where's Miyuki today?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:48.910
Hey, where's Miyuki today?

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.930
She couldn't come today.
Hey, where's Miyuki today?

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.650
I know! You had a fight!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.940
I know! You had a fight!
You're not supposed to fight.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:55.880
No fighting! Teacher said we should be friends!

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.950
Sergeant Tsujimoto. We have to go.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:58.220
Huh?

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.740
Wait!

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.440
She's leaving!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.190
What'd you do that for?

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.390
We have work to do.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.750
We don't have time
to play around.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:12.960
Interacting with the community is
part of our job too, you know.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:17.540
Don't you think that sticking to our
schedule is more important?

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.800
After all, we've got the investigation
on top of the regular patrol.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.580
She must be worried about her
career at Headquarters.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.980
But here at Bokuto we've got
our own way of doing things.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.740
I don't believe her!

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.650
Going on about the schedules
and the shifts!

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.750
If she thinks only in terms of logic,
she's got another thing coming!

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.730
Miyuki! Are you listening to me?

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.090
I am!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.930
But I'm starting to agree with
what the Inspector's saying.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.070
You're taking
her side?

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.460
That's not what I meant.
Here, look.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.740
What?

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.640
It's the Headquarters' database.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.270
I can access anything
from here.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:57.710
So?

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:00.180
She pulled a lot of strings...

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.610
...just to get
this approved.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.310
It shows how much
she trusts me.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:10.910
She's got to be staking her entire
career on this case.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:13.320
It won't be pretty
for her...

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.550
...if the criminals
aren't caught.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:21.160
She didn't say a word about
any of that to us.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:26.030
I guess that's just
not her style.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:33.880
Miyuki?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.310
Yeah?

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.840
You and I...

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.380
...we make a great
team, huh?

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.180
What are you going
on about?

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:45.850
Do you think anybody but me
would be your partner?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.890
Yeah, guess
you're right.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:56.860
These are all the files and reports
on the luxury car thefts.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:02.400
I didn't expect you to bring them here
in person, Inspector.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.510
This case means
a lot to me.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:11.570
If it's not solved soon, everyone's
future will be on the line.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:15.550
Yes, sir. I understand.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.760
Did you put Inspector Kinoshita
on this case?

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.790
Yes. She's a
good cop.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:27.860
I think she'll be a good influence
on your officers.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:28.800
Chief.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.700
Chief.
Yes?

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.670
What do you think
of this town?

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.430
It's a good
place.

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:41.870
I think so, too. But people can't
always stay in the same place.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.920
Especially people
with ambition.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.350
Yes.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:51.850
I want those women of yours
to become good cops, too.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.990
Sir!

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:23.650
At present we don't have
many leads.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:31.030
However, it's clear that these thefts
are meticulously planned.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:35.070
It's likely that there is more than
one perpetrator involved.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:41.040
A white van has been spotted
at the crime scenes.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:46.800
I want you to follow all leads
involving a white van.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.320
"Shopping Market"

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:01.790
Well, I can't see
any white vans.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:05.300
Do you really think this is the
way to catch the criminals?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.760
We're doing everything
we can.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.270
Now we'll just have to wait.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.930
Natsumi!

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.740
Long time, no see!

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:14.170
If it isn't Saori!

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.900
My mentor, Natsumi!

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.940
Oh? You're not with
Miyuki today?

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.640
No, not
today.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.150
This is Inspector Kinoshita.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.910
Inspector?!

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:26.920
Wow! I've never met anybody
so high up before!

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:34.420
Saori, have you noticed a white van
hanging around any parking lots?

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:36.790
A van?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:37.800
No.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.830
Oh.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.530
Was there a crime, Natsumi?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.270
Well... uh...

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.930
Oh, I understand!

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:50.700
If I come across a suspicious-looking white
van, I'll be sure to call you right away!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.470
If there's anything else I can do, you
just let me know! I'd love to help!

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:55.770
Thanks!

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.350
Her dream is to become a
policewoman one day.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:02.250
It's good to have enthusiastic
recruits joining the force.

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:08.350
But the reality of being a
cop is a different thing.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:09.200
Um...

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.360
Um...
Yes?

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:17.870
Is it true that you'll have to take respon-
sibility if this case isn't solved?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.900
Perhaps. Why?

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:25.200
It's just that you don't seem very
uptight, considering that.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:29.010
In fact, I want to solve this case
as quickly as possible...

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.210
...but not for my
own sake.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:35.120
Cars are still being
stolen.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:38.280
I don't know how long
this will go on.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:41.090
But the next time, someone
could get hurt...

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.180
...or even...

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.590
Anyway, I want to catch
them before that.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:51.360
It's not for the sake of my career.
But because it's my job.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.110
Kobayakawa.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.910
Nakajima.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.750
Nakajima.
Don't get too caught up in this.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.510
Thanks.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.620
It's great.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.690
It's great.
How's it going?

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:10.760
How's it going?

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.160
I've just about got everything.
How's it going?

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.630
The criminals only target
particular makes of cars.

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:21.930
So I'm tracking down the owners of such
cars, and finding out where they park.

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.960
What do you think?

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:53.130
What do you think?
I'm not sure.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.870
Inspector!

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.500
Yes.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:06.410
Attention all units. Please
state your position.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:07.910
Let's follow them!

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.210
Sergeant Tsujimoto.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:13.480
I'm sure those two are the criminals
we're looking for.

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:15.880
That's why I want
to do this right.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:19.580
If we chase them it could end
up in a serious accident.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:20.990
But...

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.550
But...
I'm not going to let them escape.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:27.360
That's why I'm going
to need your help.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.270
Bokuto Unit 6 here. We're at the Azuma
Street Commercial District.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:36.070
Come in. I'm at the intersection
of Aiaibashi.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:41.200
Bokuto Unit 11 here. We're at 3rd
street in the 6th district.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.720
Sergeant Kobayakawa.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.880
Yes!

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:49.610
I want to block off all the other
routes the white van can take.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:50.520
Over.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:54.390
Roger. Please get into position.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.690
I'll go too.

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:58.320
I'll go too.
Thanks.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.330
We're counting on you, Miyuki.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:05.770
Turn right up there.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:10.870
Bokuto Unit 6! Four streets up, head
west from Kuramae Bridge Street.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.880
Block them off in front of
the elementary school!

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.010
Roger!

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:26.620
Suspect sighted. Heading toward Komagata
Bridge right from the 2nd district.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.860
They're heading
west.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.630
Probably going to pass
Asakusa Street.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.170
Not if we can
help it!

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.400
We'll chase them down a dead
end, and stop them!

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.870
Nakajima!

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.670
Roger! I'm on it.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:55.960
There they go, Tsujimoto.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:17:00.720
Roger! I'll handle it from here!

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.370
Don't do anything dangerous.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:09.330
I won't.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.100
You're not coming
this way!

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:34.560
Give yourselves up.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.350
Damn!

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:53.040
Block the way,
Tsujimoto!

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:53.450
Huh?!

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.410
Huh?!
Wha?!

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:54.570
Lucky for us he's
a skilled driver.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:56.080
Are you okay?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.600
Are you okay?
Why did you do that?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.800
I was only doing the
same as you.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.470
Police have to protect
citizens, right?

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.580
Right!

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:23.390
So unfortunately
they escaped.

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:29.130
But we've learned quite a
bit about their M.O.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:35.810
We will take the information and devise
a new strategy for apprehending them.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:41.350
All I ask is that everyone keep their
eyes peeled. That's it.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.290
Oh, Kobayakawa.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.430
Oh, Kobayakawa.
Yes?

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:46.490
Yes?

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:51.050
Your coordination was very impressive.
Yes?

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:56.400
Not at all. Access to Headquarters'
databases made it possible.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:20:01.300
I'm going back to headquarters to develop
a revised plan of attack.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.510
Sergeant Tsujimoto.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.210
Yes?

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:07.980
I really enjoyed working
with you.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:10.650
What would you think of coming
to headquarters?

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:14.310
You could do it.
Think it over.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.550
I'll be in touch
later.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:23.780
Headquarters?

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.200
Miyuki?

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.430
What made you decide you wanted
to become a policewoman?

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.700
What makes you ask a thing
like that out of the blue?

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.840
Hmm.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.210
What about you?

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:43.340
What made you
want to?

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:46.950
Because it's
so cool!

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.510
Sounds just
like you!

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:58.960
I'm going to go.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.830
I know.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:06.440
We can't go on like this forever,
no matter how much fun it is.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.510
I've got to find
my own path.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:12.300
That's right.

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.310
Bye.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:30.760
<i>And what is it that</i>
<i>I have to do...</i>

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.530
<i>... I wonder?</i>

00:21:55.250 --> 00:22:01.590
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:11.500
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:18.400
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:28.250
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:42.490
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:50.780
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:59.420
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.650 --> 00:23:07.490
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:17.070
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:24.510
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:27.740
"Today Launched!"

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:33.680
You must be the sidekick of my
rival, Home Run Girl!

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.980
Oh, Strike Man!

00:23:36.590 --> 00:23:41.460
Take this, my special Tornado
forklift crusher!

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:43.890
Wait a minute!

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:46.290
Next time on You're Under
Arrest, File 50...

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:48.830
...The Investigation at
Bokuto Station.

00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:50.900
Come on, I'm ready!
